{"chunk_id": "e652e9b2e890", "text": "After defeating his half\u2011brother Kubera and seizing the celestial Pushpaka chariot, the arrogant Rakshasa king Dashagriva (later Ravana) travels in triumph until the vehicle halts at Mount Kailasha, where Shiva is sporting. Nandi, Shiva\u2019s attendant, bars his way and is mocked by Dashagriva for his monkey-like form. In anger Nandi prophesies that monkey warriors will one day destroy the demon\u2019s race\u2014a mythic foreshadowing of the Vanara allies of Rama. Enraged, Dashagriva attempts to uproot Kailasha itself. Shiva effortlessly pins him beneath the mountain with a toe. After a thousand years of hymns and penance, Shiva releases him and grants him the name \u201cRavana,\u201d meaning \u201che who makes the worlds cry out,\u201d explaining the legendary origin of the demon king\u2019s name.\nRavana mocks Nandi at Kailasa, attempts to lift the mountain, is crushed by Shiva\u2019s toe, and earns the name Ravana after his world\u2011shaking cry.\nThemes: hubris and punishment, divine power of Shiva, prophecy of monkey warriors, origin of Ravana's name", "vector": [0.0039159758016467094, -0.03449006378650665, 0.012046064250171185, 0.001968037337064743, -0.008917302824556828, 0.011871871538460255, -0.031274206936359406, -0.0257804524153471, -0.029532285407185555, -0.01768721267580986, 0.019656924530863762, 0.0005644498742185533, 0.02101026475429535, -0.0004815410648006946, -0.005765093490481377, 0.00034545338712632656, 0.03537442535161972, -0.021787431091070175, 0.02571345493197441, -0.009439880028367043, -0.004458651412278414, 0.004582596011459827, -0.01838398166000843, -0.022832583636045456, -0.028889114037156105, 0.011208601295948029, 0.028111949563026428, -0.028379937633872032, 0.021626638248562813, -0.03030945174396038, -0.017352227121591568, 0.003865727921947837, 0.0027703267987817526, 0.003180683357641101, -0.03416847810149193, -0.013077817857265472, -0.0060833292081952095, -0.00721557904034853, 0.014337361790239